# contact-form.ine — a realistic contact form written with ONLY the current
# dictionary vocabulary (page, header, logo, container, card-group, card,
# section, button, footer, title/text).
#
# Evidence-collection experiment (PLAN mission 71): feed the field-kind
# vocabulary decision with real-program data. A contact form needs name,
# email, a message textarea, checkboxes/consent, and a submit control; this
# program shows what that intent reduces to under the declared schema.
# Every line the vocabulary could not guide is flagged with `vocab gap:`
# and listed in .agent/NOTES.md ("## Mission 71").

make page
page title "Contact us"

make header
header inside page
make logo
logo text "Ine"
logo inside header

# A form is labeled fields plus a submit row. The dictionary's only grouping
# inside a container is a card-group of cards, so every field becomes a card
# and each field row one card-group.
make fields container
fields inside page

# A form has several field rows; each row is a card-group, and the rows sit
# inside the container (the dictionary's only grouping inside a container is a
# card-group of cards).
make identity card-group
identity inside fields
make message_row card-group
message_row inside fields
make consent card-group
consent inside fields

make 6 card

# Row 1: the three short text-like fields (name, email, topic).
group identity_fields = card-1 card-2 card-3
identity_fields inside identity
card-1 title "Full name"
card-1 text "Your name"
# vocab gap: no input kind. A card's `text` is display content, not an
# editable value — there is no field, no value/placeholder distinction, no
# required/optional marker, and no way to attach the field to a submit.

card-2 title "Email address"
card-2 text "you@example.com"
# vocab gap: no field type, so no email/format validation; the address is
# literal text the renderer prints, not a value a person can enter.

card-3 title "Topic"
card-3 text "General enquiry"
# vocab gap: no select/option-set kind and no `choice` value in use, so the
# alternative topics (Support, Sales) cannot be listed as options; only one
# literal string fits.

# Row 2: the message body, which needs a multi-line control.
group message_field = card-4
message_field inside message_row
card-4 title "Message"
card-4 text "How can we help?"
# vocab gap: no textarea kind — there is no multi-line field, no character
# count, and no resize/rows property. A single string is the whole surface.

# Row 3: consent checkboxes.
group consent_fields = card-5 card-6
consent_fields inside consent
card-5 title "Newsletter"
card-5 text "Unchecked"
card-6 title "I accept the terms"
card-6 text "Unchecked"
# vocab gap: no checkbox kind, no boolean value, no checked/unchecked state,
# and no label-for association — "Unchecked" is display text, not a value
# the runtime can toggle.

# The submit control: buttons belong inside sections, so the action row is a
# section-level strip rather than a row inside the field container.
make actions section
actions title "Send"
actions inside page
make send button
send text "Send message"
send inside actions
# vocab gap: no submit semantics, no disabled/enabled state, no validation or
# error surface, and no navigation target. The dictionary suggests
# `button label`, but renderers surface `text` — writing this form exposes
# that the suggested property and the rendered one disagree.

make footer
footer text "Ine — contact-form experiment"
footer inside page

say page title
